   "evidence": "The temporary test parked a real fixture delivery, resumed it, and used the existing fault injector to record the durable cancellation marker and simulate termination at delivery-pushed before cleanup. Reopening the factory reproduced the stale metadata. Startup recognizes `run.error?.startsWith(\"cancelled by\")`, but scheduler.ts:44-47 updates only status and finishedAt, preserving state_json. Normal cancellation explicitly clears githubWait in engine.ts:325-327. Base had the same startup status update but no githubWait field; HEAD introduces the metadata without equivalent recovery cleanup. The claim overstates UI impact: RunsTable.tsx:47 and RunDetail.tsx:315 both require status === \"queued\", so cancelled runs do not render the wait line."
